tux.png: the Tux overlay of linuxfs's volume icon.

Tux, the Linux penguin, by Larry Ewing (lewing@isc.tamu.edu), made with The GIMP. His terms: "Permission to use
and/or modify this image is granted provided you acknowledge me lewing@isc.tamu.edu and The GIMP if someone asks."
The vector version this PNG is rendered from is by Larry Ewing, Simon Budig and Garrett LeSage.

Provenance:
- Source: Wikimedia Commons, File:Tux.svg (https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tux.svg), revision of
  2026-04-27T13:31:19Z, SVG SHA-1 93e62d591aa1bad2fb12edacd0a1919e0fdf9345; credited there to
  https://isc.tamu.edu/~lewing/linux/, http://www.home.unix-ag.org/simon/penguin/ and https://github.com/garrett/Tux.
- Downloaded 2026-11-25 as Wikimedia's own 960-pixel rendering, unchanged:
  https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Tux.svg/960px-Tux.svg.png
- 960 x 1138, 8-bit RGBA (transparent background), 223939 bytes.
- SHA-256 a4bd591c958d147cfab5babbaae9d1eb91dc8ce0f38b5402f42cb0ad67c0f598

How it is used: the pkg installs it beside linuxfs-volicon (tools/volicon.c), which the postinstall runs on the target
Mac to draw it into the lower-right corner of that Mac's own External.icns (IOStorageFamily.kext), writing each
macfuse_<fs>.fs bundle's Contents/Resources/linuxfs.icns. No Apple artwork, and no composite, is in this repo or the pkg.
